{"title_zh":"中国各地的饮食","subtitle_zh":"从北方的面到南方的早茶","title_en":"Food Across China","subtitle_en":"From Northern Noodles to Southern Morning Tea","author":"Text and translation by Claude (Anthropic)","type":"meta"}
{"type":"p","id":"intro","segs":[{"en":"China is a huge country. Its regions differ in climate, landscape and history, so people in different places eat very different things.","tok":[["中国","Zhōngguó"],["很","hěn"],["大","dà"],"，",["各个","gègè"],["地方","dìfang"],["的","de"],["气候","qìhòu"],"、",["环境","huánjìng"],["和","hé"],["历史","lìshǐ"],["都","dōu"],["不","bù"],["一样","yīyàng"],"，",["所以","suǒyǐ"],["人们","rénmen"],["吃","chī"],["的","de"],["东西","dōngxi"],["也","yě"],["很","hěn"],["不","bù"],["一样","yīyàng"],"。"]},{"en":"Some say that in China the taste of the food changes every few hundred kilometres.","tok":[["有","yǒu"],["人","rén"],["说","shuō"],"，",["在","zài"],["中国","Zhōngguó"],"，",["每","měi"],["走","zǒu"],["几","jǐ"],["百","bǎi"],["公里","gōnglǐ"],"，",["饭菜","fàncài"],["的","de"],["味道","wèidao"],["就","jiù"],["会","huì"],["变","biàn"],"。"]},{"en":"Chinese people often speak of the “Eight Great Cuisines”, eight famous regional styles: Shandong, Sichuan, Cantonese, Jiangsu, Fujian, Zhejiang, Hunan and Anhui cooking.","tok":[["中国","Zhōngguó"],["人","rén"],["常","cháng"],["说","shuō"],"“",["八大菜系","bā dà càixì","the Eight Great Cuisines","J"],"”","，",["意思","yìsi"],["是","shì"],["八","bā"],["个","gè"],["有名","yǒumíng"],["的","de"],["地方","dìfang"],["菜","cài"],"：",["鲁菜","Lǔcài","Shandong cuisine","J"],"、",["川菜","Chuāncài","Sichuan cuisine","J"],"、",["粤菜","Yuècài","Cantonese cuisine","J"],"、",["苏菜","Sūcài","Jiangsu cuisine","J"],"、",["闽菜","Mǐncài","Fujian cuisine","J"],"、",["浙菜","Zhècài","Zhejiang cuisine","J"],"、",["湘菜","Xiāngcài","Hunan cuisine","J"],["和","hé"],["徽菜","Huīcài","Anhui cuisine","J"],"。"]},{"en":"Of course, China has far more than eight regional cuisines.","tok":[["当然","dāngrán"],"，",["中国","Zhōngguó"],["的","de"],["地方","dìfang"],["菜","cài"],["远远","yuǎnyuǎn","far (more)"],["不止","bùzhǐ","more than"],["八","bā"],["种","zhǒng"],"。"]},{"en":"This article takes you on a tour to see what makes the food of each part of China special.","tok":[["这","zhè"],["篇","piān"],["文章","wénzhāng"],["就","jiù"],["带","dài"],["你","nǐ"],["去","qù"],["看看","kànkan"],["中国","Zhōngguó"],["各地","gèdì"],["的","de"],["饮食","yǐnshí","food and drink, diet"],["有","yǒu"],["什么","shénme"],["特点","tèdiǎn"],"。"]}],"zh":"中国很大，各个地方的气候、环境和历史都不一样，所以人们吃的东西也很不一样。有人说，在中国，每走几百公里，饭菜的味道就会变。中国人常说“八大菜系”，意思是八个有名的地方菜：鲁菜、川菜、粤菜、苏菜、闽菜、浙菜、湘菜和徽菜。当然，中国的地方菜远远不止八种。这篇文章就带你去看看中国各地的饮食有什么特点。"}
{"type":"h2","id":"h-north-south","segs":[{"en":"Noodles in the North, Rice in the South","tok":[["北方","běifāng"],["的","de"],["面","miàn"],"，",["南方","nánfāng"],["的","de"],["米","mǐ"]]}],"zh":"北方的面，南方的米"}
{"type":"p","id":"ns-1","segs":[{"en":"One of the biggest differences between northern and southern China is the staple food.","tok":[["中国","Zhōngguó"],["北方","běifāng"],["和","hé"],["南方","nánfāng"],["最","zuì"],["大","dà"],["的","de"],["区别","qūbié"],["之一","zhīyī","one of"],"，",["是","shì"],["主食","zhǔshí","staple food"],["不同","bùtóng"],"。"]},{"en":"Northern winters are cold and there is less rain, which suits wheat, so northerners mainly eat wheat-based foods such as noodles, dumplings, stuffed buns and plain steamed buns.","tok":[["北方","běifāng"],["冬天","dōngtiān"],["冷","lěng"],"，",["雨水","yǔshuǐ","rainfall"],["比较","bǐjiào"],["少","shǎo"],"，",["适合","shìhé"],["种","zhòng"],["小麦","xiǎomài","wheat"],"，",["所以","suǒyǐ"],["北方","běifāng"],["人","rén"],["主要","zhǔyào"],["吃","chī"],["面食","miànshí","wheat-based foods","J"],"，",["比如","bǐrú"],["面条","miàntiáo"],"、",["饺子","jiǎozi","dumplings"],"、",["包子","bāozi","steamed stuffed buns"],["和","hé"],["馒头","mántou","plain steamed buns","J"],"。"]},{"en":"The south is warm and rainy, ideal for growing rice, so southerners can hardly go a day without it.","tok":[["南方","nánfāng"],["天气","tiānqì"],["暖和","nuǎnhuo"],"，",["雨水","yǔshuǐ","rainfall"],["多","duō"],"，",["适合","shìhé"],["种","zhòng"],["水稻","shuǐdào","rice (the crop)"],"，",["所以","suǒyǐ"],["南方","nánfāng"],["人","rén"],["每天","měitiān"],["都","dōu"],["离不开","líbukāi","can't do without"],["米饭","mǐfàn"],"。"]}],"zh":"中国北方和南方最大的区别之一，是主食不同。北方冬天冷，雨水比较少，适合种小麦，所以北方人主要吃面食，比如面条、饺子、包子和馒头。南方天气暖和，雨水多，适合种水稻，所以南方人每天都离不开米饭。"}
{"type":"p","id":"ns-2","segs":[{"en":"In the north there is a huge variety of wheat-based dishes.","tok":[["在","zài"],["北方","běifāng"],"，",["面食","miànshí","wheat-based foods","J"],["的","de"],["种类","zhǒnglèi"],["非常","fēicháng"],["多","duō"],"。"]},{"en":"People in Shanxi are especially good at making noodles; it is said the province has several hundred kinds of wheat dishes.","tok":[["山西","Shānxī","Shanxi (province)","N"],["人","rén"],["特别","tèbié"],["会","huì"],["做","zuò"],["面","miàn"],"，",["据说","jùshuō","it is said"],["山西","Shānxī","Shanxi (province)","N"],["的","de"],["面食","miànshí","wheat-based foods","J"],["有","yǒu"],["几","jǐ"],["百","bǎi"],["种","zhǒng"],"。"]},{"en":"The best known is knife-shaved noodles: the cook holds a big lump of dough in one hand and a knife in the other, and quickly shaves the dough strip by strip straight into boiling water.","tok":[["其中","qízhōng"],["最","zuì"],["有名","yǒumíng"],["的","de"],["是","shì"],["刀削面","dāoxiāomiàn","knife-shaved noodles","J"],"：",["厨师","chúshī","chef, cook"],["一","yī"],["手","shǒu"],["拿","ná"],["着","zhe"],["一","yī"],["大","dà"],["块","kuài"],["面","miàn"],"，",["一","yī"],["手","shǒu"],["拿","ná"],["着","zhe"],["刀","dāo"],"，",["很","hěn"],["快","kuài"],["地","de"],["把","bǎ"],["面","miàn"],["一","yī"],["片","piàn"],["一","yī"],["片","piàn"],["削","xiāo","to shave, to pare"],["到","dào"],["开水","kāishuǐ"],["里","lǐ"],"。"]},{"en":"Lanzhou beef noodle soup is famous too. Locals say that in a good bowl the broth is clear, the radish white, the chili oil red, the coriander green and the noodles yellow.","tok":[["兰州","Lánzhōu","Lanzhou","N"],["牛肉面","niúròumiàn","beef noodle soup","J"],["也","yě"],["很","hěn"],["有名","yǒumíng"],"，",["当地","dāngdì","local"],["人","rén"],["说","shuō"],"，",["一","yī"],["碗","wǎn"],["好","hǎo"],["的","de"],["牛肉面","niúròumiàn","beef noodle soup","J"],"，",["汤","tāng"],["要","yào"],["清","qīng","clear"],"，",["萝卜","luóbo","radish"],["要","yào"],["白","bái"],"，",["辣椒油","làjiāoyóu","chili oil","J"],["要","yào"],["红","hóng"],"，",["香菜","xiāngcài","coriander"],["要","yào"],["绿","lǜ"],"，",["面","miàn"],["要","yào"],["黄","huáng"],"。"]}],"zh":"在北方，面食的种类非常多。山西人特别会做面，据说山西的面食有几百种。其中最有名的是刀削面：厨师一手拿着一大块面，一手拿着刀，很快地把面一片一片削到开水里。兰州牛肉面也很有名，当地人说，一碗好的牛肉面，汤要清，萝卜要白，辣椒油要红，香菜要绿，面要黄。"}
{"type":"p","id":"ns-3","segs":[{"en":"Southerners don't just eat plain rice; they turn it into many other foods, such as rice noodles, rice cakes and zongzi.","tok":[["南方","nánfāng"],["人","rén"],["不但","bùdàn"],["吃","chī"],["米饭","mǐfàn"],"，",["还","hái"],["用","yòng"],["大米","dàmǐ","rice (grain)"],["做","zuò"],["出","chū"],["很多","hěnduō"],["别的","biéde"],["食物","shíwù"],"，",["比如","bǐrú"],["米粉","mǐfěn","rice noodles","J"],"、",["年糕","niángāo","rice cake","J"],["和","hé"],["粽子","zòngzi","zongzi, sticky rice wrapped in leaves","J"],"。"]},{"en":"In Guangxi and Hunan, many people's favourite breakfast is a hot bowl of rice noodles.","tok":[["在","zài"],["广西","Guǎngxī","Guangxi","N"],["和","hé"],["湖南","Húnán","Hunan","N"],"，",["很多","hěnduō"],["人","rén"],["早上","zǎoshang"],["最","zuì"],["喜欢","xǐhuan"],["吃","chī"],["一","yī"],["碗","wǎn"],["热","rè"],["米粉","mǐfěn","rice noodles","J"],"。"]},{"en":"Of course, now that travel is easy, northerners often eat rice and southerners love noodles too, so the difference is not as big as it once was.","tok":[["当然","dāngrán"],"，",["现在","xiànzài"],["交通","jiāotōng"],["方便","fāngbiàn"],["了","le"],"，",["北方","běifāng"],["人","rén"],["也","yě"],["常","cháng"],["吃","chī"],["米饭","mǐfàn"],"，",["南方","nánfāng"],["人","rén"],["也","yě"],["爱","ài"],["吃","chī"],["面条","miàntiáo"],"，",["这种","zhèzhǒng"],["区别","qūbié"],["已经","yǐjīng"],["不","bù"],["像","xiàng"],["以前","yǐqián"],["那么","nàme"],["大","dà"],["了","le"],"。"]}],"zh":"南方人不但吃米饭，还用大米做出很多别的食物，比如米粉、年糕和粽子。在广西和湖南，很多人早上最喜欢吃一碗热米粉。当然，现在交通方便了，北方人也常吃米饭，南方人也爱吃面条，这种区别已经不像以前那么大了。"}
{"type":"h2","id":"h-sichuan","segs":[{"en":"Sichuan Cuisine: Numbing and Hot","tok":[["川菜","Chuāncài","Sichuan cuisine","J"],"：",["又","yòu"],["麻","má","numbing (spicy)"],["又","yòu"],["辣","là"]]}],"zh":"川菜：又麻又辣"}
{"type":"p","id":"sc-1","segs":[{"en":"Speaking of spicy food, the first thing many people think of is Sichuan cooking, known as chuancai.","tok":[["说到","shuōdào"],["辣","là"],"，",["很多","hěnduō"],["人","rén"],["第一","dìyī"],["个","gè"],["想到","xiǎngdào"],["的","de"],["就","jiù"],["是","shì"],["四川","Sìchuān","Sichuan","N"],["菜","cài"],"，",["也","yě"],["叫","jiào"],["川菜","Chuāncài","Sichuan cuisine","J"],"。"]},{"en":"Its two great features are “ma”, numbing, and “la”, hot.","tok":[["川菜","Chuāncài","Sichuan cuisine","J"],["最","zuì"],["大","dà"],["的","de"],["特点","tèdiǎn"],["是","shì"],"“",["麻","má","numbing (spicy)"],"”",["和","hé"],"“",["辣","là"],"”","。"]},{"en":"The heat comes from chili peppers, the numbing from Sichuan pepper.","tok":["“",["辣","là"],"”",["来自","láizì"],["辣椒","làjiāo","chili pepper"],"，","“",["麻","má","numbing (spicy)"],"”",["来自","láizì"],["花椒","huājiāo","Sichuan pepper","J"],"。"]},{"en":"When you bite on Sichuan pepper your tongue tingles, almost as if there were electricity in it.","tok":[["花椒","huājiāo","Sichuan pepper","J"],["吃","chī"],["到","dào"],["嘴","zuǐ"],["里","lǐ"],"，",["舌头","shétou","tongue"],["会","huì"],["有","yǒu"],["一","yī"],["种","zhǒng"],["麻麻","mámá","tingling"],["的","de"],["感觉","gǎnjué"],"，",["好像","hǎoxiàng"],["有","yǒu"],["电","diàn"],["一样","yīyàng"],"。"]},{"en":"Many foreigners find it very strange the first time, but after a while they slowly come to love the taste.","tok":[["很多","hěnduō"],["外国","wàiguó"],["朋友","péngyou"],["第一","dìyī"],["次","cì"],["吃","chī"],["花椒","huājiāo","Sichuan pepper","J"],"，",["都","dōu"],["觉得","juéde"],["很","hěn"],["奇怪","qíguài"],"，",["可是","kěshì"],["吃","chī"],["多","duō"],["了","le"],["以后","yǐhòu"],"，",["就","jiù"],["会","huì"],["慢慢","mànmàn"],["喜欢","xǐhuan"],["上","shàng"],["这种","zhèzhǒng"],["味道","wèidao"],"。"]}],"zh":"说到辣，很多人第一个想到的就是四川菜，也叫川菜。川菜最大的特点是“麻”和“辣”。“辣”来自辣椒，“麻”来自花椒。花椒吃到嘴里，舌头会有一种麻麻的感觉，好像有电一样。很多外国朋友第一次吃花椒，都觉得很奇怪，可是吃多了以后，就会慢慢喜欢上这种味道。"}
{"type":"p","id":"sc-2","segs":[{"en":"Famous Sichuan dishes include mapo tofu, kung pao chicken, fish boiled in chili oil and twice-cooked pork.","tok":[["有名","yǒumíng"],["的","de"],["川菜","Chuāncài","Sichuan cuisine","J"],["有","yǒu"],["麻婆豆腐","mápó dòufu","mapo tofu","J"],"、",["宫保鸡丁","gōngbǎo jīdīng","kung pao chicken","J"],"、",["水煮鱼","shuǐzhǔyú","fish boiled in chili oil","J"],["和","hé"],["回锅肉","huíguōròu","twice-cooked pork","J"],"。"]},{"en":"Even more famous is the hotpot of Chengdu and Chongqing.","tok":[["成都","Chéngdū","Chengdu","N"],["和","hé"],["重庆","Chóngqìng","Chongqing","N"],["的","de"],["火锅","huǒguō","hotpot","J"],["更","gèng"],["是","shì"],["有名","yǒumíng"],"。"]},{"en":"A big pot of bright red broth full of chilies and Sichuan pepper sits in the middle; everyone sits around it, cooking meat and vegetables in it, eating and chatting in a lively crowd.","tok":[["一","yī"],["大","dà"],["锅","guō","pot"],["红红","hónghóng","bright red"],["的","de"],["汤","tāng"],"，",["里面","lǐmiàn"],["放","fàng"],["满","mǎn"],["了","le"],["辣椒","làjiāo","chili pepper"],["和","hé"],["花椒","huājiāo","Sichuan pepper","J"],"，",["大家","dàjiā"],["围","wéi"],["着","zhe"],["锅","guō","pot"],["坐","zuò"],"，",["把","bǎ"],["肉","ròu"],["和","hé"],["菜","cài"],["放","fàng"],["进去","jìnqu"],["煮","zhǔ","to boil"],"，",["一边","yībiān"],["吃","chī"],["一边","yībiān"],["聊","liáo","to chat"],"，",["非常","fēicháng"],["热闹","rènao","lively"],"。"]}],"zh":"有名的川菜有麻婆豆腐、宫保鸡丁、水煮鱼和回锅肉。成都和重庆的火锅更是有名。一大锅红红的汤，里面放满了辣椒和花椒，大家围着锅坐，把肉和菜放进去煮，一边吃一边聊，非常热闹。"}
{"type":"p","id":"sc-3","segs":[{"en":"Interestingly, the chili pepper is not native to China.","tok":[["有意思","yǒuyìsi"],["的","de"],["是","shì"],"，",["辣椒","làjiāo","chili pepper"],["并","bìng"],["不","bù"],["是","shì"],["中国","Zhōngguó"],["本来","běnlái"],["就","jiù"],["有","yǒu"],["的","de"],"。"]},{"en":"It came from the Americas and only reached China in the later part of the Ming dynasty.","tok":[["辣椒","làjiāo","chili pepper"],["来自","láizì"],["美洲","Měizhōu","the Americas","N"],"，",["大概","dàgài"],["在","zài"],["明朝","Míngcháo","the Ming dynasty (1368–1644)","N"],["后期","hòuqī","later period"],["才","cái"],["传","chuán"],["到","dào"],["中国","Zhōngguó"],"。"]},{"en":"In other words, Sichuan food has only been this hot for a few hundred years.","tok":[["也","yě"],["就","jiù"],["是","shì"],["说","shuō"],"，",["川菜","Chuāncài","Sichuan cuisine","J"],["变","biàn"],["得","de"],["这么","zhème"],["辣","là"],"，",["其实","qíshí"],["只有","zhǐyǒu"],["几","jǐ"],["百","bǎi"],["年","nián"],["的","de"],["历史","lìshǐ"],"。"]},{"en":"Besides the Sichuanese, people from Hunan are also famous for handling chili.","tok":[["除了","chúle"],["四川","Sìchuān","Sichuan","N"],["人","rén"],"，",["湖南","Húnán","Hunan","N"],["人","rén"],["也","yě"],["特别","tèbié"],["能","néng"],["吃","chī"],["辣","là"],"。"]},{"en":"But Hunan heat is different: it is fragrant and hot, often a little sour, without much of the numbing tingle.","tok":[["不过","bùguò"],"，",["湘菜","Xiāngcài","Hunan cuisine","J"],["的","de"],["辣","là"],["和","hé"],["川菜","Chuāncài","Sichuan cuisine","J"],["不","bù"],["太","tài"],["一样","yīyàng"],"，",["它","tā"],["常常","chángcháng"],["是","shì"],["又","yòu"],["香","xiāng"],["又","yòu"],["辣","là"],"，",["还","hái"],["带","dài"],["一点儿","yīdiǎnr"],["酸","suān"],"，",["但是","dànshì"],["不","bù"],["太","tài"],["麻","má","numbing (spicy)"],"。"]}],"zh":"有意思的是，辣椒并不是中国本来就有的。辣椒来自美洲，大概在明朝后期才传到中国。也就是说，川菜变得这么辣，其实只有几百年的历史。除了四川人，湖南人也特别能吃辣。不过，湘菜的辣和川菜不太一样，它常常是又香又辣，还带一点儿酸，但是不太麻。"}
{"type":"h2","id":"h-cantonese","segs":[{"en":"Cantonese Food and Morning Tea","tok":[["粤菜","Yuècài","Cantonese cuisine","J"],["和","hé"],["早茶","zǎochá","morning tea (a dim sum meal)","J"]]}],"zh":"粤菜和早茶"}
{"type":"p","id":"yue-1","segs":[{"en":"Yuecai is Cantonese food, probably the best-known Chinese cooking in the world.","tok":[["粤菜","Yuècài","Cantonese cuisine","J"],["就","jiù"],["是","shì"],["广东","Guǎngdōng","Guangdong","N"],["菜","cài"],"，",["在","zài"],["世界","shìjiè"],["上","shàng"],["可能","kěnéng"],["是","shì"],["最","zuì"],["有名","yǒumíng"],["的","de"],["中国","Zhōngguó"],["菜","cài"],"。"]},{"en":"That is because many Cantonese people moved abroad long ago and took their home cooking all over the world.","tok":[["这","zhè"],["是","shì"],["因为","yīnwèi"],["很","hěn"],["早","zǎo"],["以前","yǐqián"],"，",["就","jiù"],["有","yǒu"],["很多","hěnduō"],["广东","Guǎngdōng","Guangdong","N"],["人","rén"],["到","dào"],["国外","guówài"],["生活","shēnghuó"],"，",["他们","tāmen"],["把","bǎ"],["家乡","jiāxiāng"],["菜","cài"],["带","dài"],["到","dào"],["了","le"],["世界","shìjiè"],["各地","gèdì"],"。"]},{"en":"Cantonese cooking is almost the opposite of Sichuan: it is not very hot, its flavours are light, and it cares a great deal about fresh ingredients.","tok":[["粤菜","Yuècài","Cantonese cuisine","J"],["的","de"],["特点","tèdiǎn"],["和","hé"],["川菜","Chuāncài","Sichuan cuisine","J"],["差不多","chàbuduō"],["相反","xiāngfǎn"],"：",["它","tā"],["不","bù"],["太","tài"],["辣","là"],"，",["味道","wèidao"],["比较","bǐjiào"],["清淡","qīngdàn","light, mild"],"，",["非常","fēicháng"],["重视","zhòngshì"],["食材","shícái","ingredients"],["是否","shìfǒu"],["新鲜","xīnxiān"],"。"]},{"en":"The Cantonese believe good ingredients need little seasoning: steam them simply and you taste what they really are.","tok":[["广东","Guǎngdōng","Guangdong","N"],["人","rén"],["认为","rènwéi"],"，",["好","hǎo"],["的","de"],["食材","shícái","ingredients"],["不","bù"],["需要","xūyào"],["太","tài"],["多","duō"],["调料","tiáoliào","seasonings"],"，",["简单","jiǎndān"],["地","de"],["蒸","zhēng","to steam"],["一下","yīxià"],"，",["就","jiù"],["能","néng"],["吃","chī"],["出","chū"],["它","tā"],["本来","běnlái"],["的","de"],["味道","wèidao"],"。"]}],"zh":"粤菜就是广东菜，在世界上可能是最有名的中国菜。这是因为很早以前，就有很多广东人到国外生活，他们把家乡菜带到了世界各地。粤菜的特点和川菜差不多相反：它不太辣，味道比较清淡，非常重视食材是否新鲜。广东人认为，好的食材不需要太多调料，简单地蒸一下，就能吃出它本来的味道。"}
{"type":"p","id":"yue-2","segs":[{"en":"In Guangzhou and Hong Kong many people have the habit of “drinking morning tea”.","tok":[["在","zài"],["广州","Guǎngzhōu","Guangzhou","N"],["和","hé"],["香港","Xiānggǎng","Hong Kong","N"],"，",["很多","hěnduō"],["人","rén"],["有","yǒu"],"“",["喝","hē"],["早茶","zǎochá","morning tea (a dim sum meal)","J"],"”",["的","de"],["习惯","xíguàn"],"。"]},{"en":"In the morning or at noon, family and friends go to a teahouse together, order a pot of tea and a few baskets of dim sum, and eat and talk at leisure, sometimes for two or three hours.","tok":[["早上","zǎoshang"],["或者","huòzhě"],["中午","zhōngwǔ"],"，",["家人","jiārén"],["和","hé"],["朋友","péngyou"],["一起","yīqǐ"],["去","qù"],["茶楼","chálóu","teahouse","J"],"，",["点","diǎn"],["一","yī"],["壶","hú","pot (measure word)"],["茶","chá"],"，",["再","zài"],["点","diǎn"],["几","jǐ"],["笼","lóng","steamer basket (measure word)"],["点心","diǎnxin","dim sum, snacks","J"],"，",["慢慢","mànmàn"],["吃","chī"],"，",["慢慢","mànmàn"],["聊","liáo","to chat"],"，",["有时候","yǒushíhou"],["一","yī"],["坐","zuò"],["就","jiù"],["是","shì"],["两三","liǎngsān"],["个","gè"],["小时","xiǎoshí"],"。"]},{"en":"There are many kinds of dim sum, such as shrimp dumplings, shaomai, barbecue pork buns and rice noodle rolls.","tok":[["点心","diǎnxin","dim sum, snacks","J"],["的","de"],["种类","zhǒnglèi"],["很","hěn"],["多","duō"],"，",["比如","bǐrú"],["虾饺","xiājiǎo","shrimp dumplings","J"],"、",["烧卖","shāomai","shaomai dumplings","J"],"、",["叉烧包","chāshāobāo","barbecue pork bun","J"],["和","hé"],["肠粉","chángfěn","rice noodle rolls","J"],"。"]},{"en":"Each portion is small and comes in a little bamboo steamer, so everyone can order several kinds and share them.","tok":[["每","měi"],["样","yàng","kind (measure word)"],["点心","diǎnxin","dim sum, snacks","J"],["都","dōu"],["很","hěn"],["小","xiǎo"],"，",["放","fàng"],["在","zài"],["小小","xiǎoxiǎo"],["的","de"],["竹","zhú","bamboo"],["笼","lóng","steamer basket (measure word)"],["里","lǐ"],"，",["所以","suǒyǐ"],["大家","dàjiā"],["可以","kěyǐ"],["多","duō"],["点","diǎn"],["几","jǐ"],["样","yàng","kind (measure word)"],"，",["一起","yīqǐ"],["分","fēn"],["着","zhe"],["吃","chī"],"。"]}],"zh":"在广州和香港，很多人有“喝早茶”的习惯。早上或者中午，家人和朋友一起去茶楼，点一壶茶，再点几笼点心，慢慢吃，慢慢聊，有时候一坐就是两三个小时。点心的种类很多，比如虾饺、烧卖、叉烧包和肠粉。每样点心都很小，放在小小的竹笼里，所以大家可以多点几样，一起分着吃。"}
{"type":"p","id":"yue-3","segs":[{"en":"The Cantonese eat an especially wide range of things; people joke that whatever flies in the sky, walks on land or swims in water, the Cantonese will dare to eat it.","tok":[["广东","Guǎngdōng","Guangdong","N"],["人","rén"],["吃","chī"],["的","de"],["东西","dōngxi"],["种类","zhǒnglèi"],["特别","tèbié"],["多","duō"],"，",["有","yǒu"],["人","rén"],["开玩笑","kāiwánxiào"],["说","shuō"],"，",["天上","tiānshàng"],["飞","fēi"],["的","de"],"、",["地上","dìshang"],["走","zǒu"],["的","de"],"、",["水","shuǐ"],["里","lǐ"],["游","yóu"],["的","de"],"，",["广东","Guǎngdōng","Guangdong","N"],["人","rén"],["都","dōu"],["敢","gǎn"],["吃","chī"],"。"]},{"en":"That is an exaggeration, but it shows how rich the range of Cantonese ingredients is.","tok":[["这","zhè"],["句","jù"],["话","huà"],["虽然","suīrán"],["有点儿","yǒudiǎnr"],["夸张","kuāzhāng","exaggerated"],"，",["但是","dànshì"],["也","yě"],["说明","shuōmíng"],["了","le"],["粤菜","Yuècài","Cantonese cuisine","J"],["的","de"],["食材","shícái","ingredients"],["非常","fēicháng"],["丰富","fēngfù"],"。"]},{"en":"The Cantonese also love slow-cooked soups: many families spend hours simmering a pot of soup, believing it is very good for the body.","tok":[["另外","lìngwài"],"，",["广东","Guǎngdōng","Guangdong","N"],["人","rén"],["很","hěn"],["喜欢","xǐhuan"],["煲汤","bāotāng","to slow-cook soup","J"],"，",["很多","hěnduō"],["家庭","jiātíng"],["会","huì"],["花","huā"],["好几","hǎojǐ"],["个","gè"],["小时","xiǎoshí"],["慢慢","mànmàn"],["煮","zhǔ","to boil"],["一","yī"],["锅","guō","pot"],["汤","tāng"],"，",["他们","tāmen"],["相信","xiāngxìn"],["这样","zhèyàng"],["的","de"],["汤","tāng"],["对","duì"],["身体","shēntǐ"],["很","hěn"],["好","hǎo"],"。"]}],"zh":"广东人吃的东西种类特别多，有人开玩笑说，天上飞的、地上走的、水里游的，广东人都敢吃。这句话虽然有点儿夸张，但是也说明了粤菜的食材非常丰富。另外，广东人很喜欢煲汤，很多家庭会花好几个小时慢慢煮一锅汤，他们相信这样的汤对身体很好。"}
{"type":"h2","id":"h-sweet-salty","segs":[{"en":"Sweet South, Salty North","tok":[["南甜北咸","nán tián běi xián","“sweet south, salty north”","I"]]}],"zh":"南甜北咸"}
{"type":"p","id":"ss-1","segs":[{"en":"Chinese people often sum up the difference in taste between north and south in four characters: nan tian bei xian, “sweet south, salty north”.","tok":[["中国","Zhōngguó"],["人","rén"],["常","cháng"],["用","yòng"],"“",["南甜北咸","nán tián běi xián","“sweet south, salty north”","I"],"”",["这","zhè"],["四","sì"],["个","gè"],["字","zì"],["来","lái"],["说","shuō"],["南北","nánběi","north and south"],["口味","kǒuwèi","taste, flavour"],["的","de"],["不同","bùtóng"],"。"]},{"en":"The saying is not entirely accurate, of course, but it captures the general picture.","tok":[["这","zhè"],["句","jù"],["话","huà"],["当然","dāngrán"],["不","bù"],["完全","wánquán"],["准确","zhǔnquè"],"，",["但是","dànshì"],["说","shuō"],["出","chū"],["了","le"],["一","yī"],["个","gè"],["大概","dàgài"],["的","de"],["情况","qíngkuàng"],"。"]}],"zh":"中国人常用“南甜北咸”这四个字来说南北口味的不同。这句话当然不完全准确，但是说出了一个大概的情况。"}
{"type":"p","id":"ss-2","segs":[{"en":"The food of Shanghai, Suzhou and Wuxi is often rather sweet.","tok":[["上海","Shànghǎi","Shanghai","N"],"、",["苏州","Sūzhōu","Suzhou","N"],["和","hé"],["无锡","Wúxī","Wuxi","N"],["一带","yīdài","area, region"],["的","de"],["菜","cài"],"，",["常常","chángcháng"],["比较","bǐjiào"],["甜","tián"],"。"]},{"en":"Shanghai's red-braised pork, for example, takes quite a lot of sugar; it is a glossy red and tastes sweet and rich.","tok":[["比如","bǐrú"],["上海","Shànghǎi","Shanghai","N"],["的","de"],["红烧肉","hóngshāoròu","red-braised pork","J"],"，",["要","yào"],["放","fàng"],["不少","bùshǎo"],["糖","táng"],"，",["颜色","yánsè"],["红","hóng"],["亮","liàng"],"，",["吃","chī"],["起来","qǐlai"],["又","yòu"],["甜","tián"],["又","yòu"],["香","xiāng"],"。"]},{"en":"Wuxi's spare ribs are sweet too.","tok":[["无锡","Wúxī","Wuxi","N"],["的","de"],["排骨","páigǔ","spare ribs"],["也","yě"],["很","hěn"],["甜","tián"],"。"]},{"en":"Many northerners eating in Shanghai for the first time wonder, “Why is there sugar in every dish?”","tok":[["很多","hěnduō"],["北方","běifāng"],["人","rén"],["第一","dìyī"],["次","cì"],["去","qù"],["上海","Shànghǎi","Shanghai","N"],["吃","chī"],["饭","fàn"],"，",["都","dōu"],["会","huì"],["奇怪","qíguài"],"：","“",["怎么","zěnme"],["每","měi"],["个","gè"],["菜","cài"],["都","dōu"],["放","fàng"],["糖","táng"],"？","”"]}],"zh":"上海、苏州和无锡一带的菜，常常比较甜。比如上海的红烧肉，要放不少糖，颜色红亮，吃起来又甜又香。无锡的排骨也很甜。很多北方人第一次去上海吃饭，都会奇怪：“怎么每个菜都放糖？”"}
{"type":"p","id":"ss-3","segs":[{"en":"Northern food, on the other hand, tends to be saltier, with more soy sauce and salt and stronger flavours.","tok":[["北方","běifāng"],["菜","cài"],["呢","ne"],"，",["常常","chángcháng"],["比较","bǐjiào"],["咸","xián","salty"],"，",["酱油","jiàngyóu","soy sauce"],["和","hé"],["盐","yán"],["放","fàng"],["得","de"],["比较","bǐjiào"],["多","duō"],"，",["味道","wèidao"],["也","yě"],["比较","bǐjiào"],["重","zhòng"],"。"]},{"en":"Dishes in the Northeast come in big portions — one plate is often enough for several people — such as guobaorou, crispy sweet-and-sour pork, and disanxian, fried potato, aubergine and green pepper.","tok":[["东北","Dōngběi","Northeast China","N"],["菜","cài"],["分量","fènliàng","portion size"],["很","hěn"],["大","dà"],"，",["一","yī"],["盘","pán"],["菜","cài"],["常常","chángcháng"],["够","gòu"],["好几","hǎojǐ"],["个","gè"],["人","rén"],["吃","chī"],"，",["比如","bǐrú"],["锅包肉","guōbāoròu","crispy sweet-and-sour pork","J"],["和","hé"],["地三鲜","dìsānxiān","fried potato, aubergine and pepper","J"],"。"]},{"en":"Shandong cooking, Lucai, has one of the longest histories of the eight great cuisines, and many dishes of the old imperial palace were influenced by it.","tok":[["山东","Shāndōng","Shandong","N"],["菜","cài"],"，",["也","yě"],["就","jiù"],["是","shì"],["鲁菜","Lǔcài","Shandong cuisine","J"],"，",["是","shì"],["八大菜系","bā dà càixì","the Eight Great Cuisines","J"],["中","zhōng"],["历史","lìshǐ"],["最","zuì"],["长","cháng"],["的","de"],["之一","zhīyī","one of"],"，",["以前","yǐqián"],["皇宫","huánggōng","imperial palace"],["里","lǐ"],["的","de"],["很多","hěnduō"],["菜","cài"],["都","dōu"],["受到","shòudào"],["了","le"],["鲁菜","Lǔcài","Shandong cuisine","J"],["的","de"],["影响","yǐngxiǎng"],"。"]}],"zh":"北方菜呢，常常比较咸，酱油和盐放得比较多，味道也比较重。东北菜分量很大，一盘菜常常够好几个人吃，比如锅包肉和地三鲜。山东菜，也就是鲁菜，是八大菜系中历史最长的之一，以前皇宫里的很多菜都受到了鲁菜的影响。"}
{"type":"p","id":"ss-4","segs":[{"en":"Shanxi people's love of vinegar is well known; some say they add a little to everything they eat.","tok":[["山西","Shānxī","Shanxi (province)","N"],["人","rén"],["爱","ài"],["吃","chī"],["醋","cù","vinegar"],["是","shì"],["出了名","chūlemíng","well known"],["的","de"],"，",["有","yǒu"],["人","rén"],["说","shuō"],"，",["山西","Shānxī","Shanxi (province)","N"],["人","rén"],["吃","chī"],["什么","shénme"],["都","dōu"],["要","yào"],["放","fàng"],["一点儿","yīdiǎnr"],["醋","cù","vinegar"],"。"]},{"en":"Tofu pudding is a fun example of regional taste.","tok":[["豆腐脑","dòufunǎo","tofu pudding","J"],["是","shì"],["一","yī"],["个","gè"],["很","hěn"],["好玩","hǎowán"],["的","de"],["例子","lìzi"],"。"]},{"en":"Many northerners eat it savoury, topped with soy sauce and other seasonings, while many southerners eat it sweet, with just sugar or syrup.","tok":[["很多","hěnduō"],["北方","běifāng"],["人","rén"],["吃","chī"],["咸","xián","salty"],["的","de"],["豆腐脑","dòufunǎo","tofu pudding","J"],"，",["上面","shàngmian"],["放","fàng"],["酱油","jiàngyóu","soy sauce"],["和","hé"],["别的","biéde"],["调料","tiáoliào","seasonings"],"；",["很多","hěnduō"],["南方","nánfāng"],["人","rén"],["却","què"],["吃","chī"],["甜","tián"],["的","de"],"，",["只","zhǐ"],["放","fàng"],["糖","táng"],["或者","huòzhě"],["糖水","tángshuǐ","syrup"],"。"]},{"en":"Every year people argue about it online, just as they argue at the Dragon Boat Festival over whether zongzi should be sweet or salty.","tok":[["每年","měinián"],["网上","wǎngshàng"],["都","dōu"],["有","yǒu"],["人","rén"],["为","wèi"],["这个","zhège"],["问题","wèntí"],["争论","zhēnglùn","to argue"],"，",["就","jiù"],["像","xiàng"],["端午节","Duānwǔjié","Dragon Boat Festival","J"],["的","de"],["时候","shíhou"],["争论","zhēnglùn","to argue"],["粽子","zòngzi","zongzi, sticky rice wrapped in leaves","J"],["是","shì"],["甜","tián"],["的","de"],["好","hǎo"],["还是","háishi"],["咸","xián","salty"],["的","de"],["好","hǎo"],["一样","yīyàng"],"。"]}],"zh":"山西人爱吃醋是出了名的，有人说，山西人吃什么都要放一点儿醋。豆腐脑是一个很好玩的例子。很多北方人吃咸的豆腐脑，上面放酱油和别的调料；很多南方人却吃甜的，只放糖或者糖水。每年网上都有人为这个问题争论，就像端午节的时候争论粽子是甜的好还是咸的好一样。"}
{"type":"h2","id":"h-table","segs":[{"en":"Customs at the Table","tok":[["饭桌","fànzhuō","dining table"],["上","shàng"],["的","de"],["习惯","xíguàn"]]}],"zh":"饭桌上的习惯"}
{"type":"p","id":"tb-1","segs":[{"en":"Unlike in many Western countries, Chinese meals are usually not one plate per person: several dishes are placed in the middle of the table and everyone shares.","tok":[["和","hé"],["很多","hěnduō"],["西方","xīfāng"],["国家","guójiā"],["不","bù"],["一样","yīyàng"],"，",["中国","Zhōngguó"],["人","rén"],["吃","chī"],["饭","fàn"],["的","de"],["时候","shíhou"],"，",["一般","yībān"],["不","bù"],["是","shì"],["每","měi"],["人","rén"],["一","yī"],["份","fèn"],"，",["而是","érshì"],["把","bǎ"],["几","jǐ"],["个","gè"],["菜","cài"],["放","fàng"],["在","zài"],["桌子","zhuōzi"],["中间","zhōngjiān"],"，",["大家","dàjiā"],["一起","yīqǐ"],["吃","chī"],"。"]},{"en":"So when ordering you have to think about everyone's tastes; ideally there is meat, fish and vegetables, plus a soup.","tok":[["所以","suǒyǐ"],"，",["点","diǎn"],["菜","cài"],["的","de"],["时候","shíhou"],["要","yào"],["考虑","kǎolǜ"],["每","měi"],["个","gè"],["人","rén"],["的","de"],["口味","kǒuwèi","taste, flavour"],"，",["最好","zuìhǎo"],["有","yǒu"],["肉","ròu"],"、",["有","yǒu"],["鱼","yú"],"、",["有","yǒu"],["蔬菜","shūcài","vegetables"],"，",["再","zài"],["来","lái"],["一","yī"],["个","gè"],["汤","tāng"],"。"]},{"en":"Many restaurants use large round tables with a revolving glass top in the middle, so everyone can easily reach every dish with their chopsticks.","tok":[["很多","hěnduō"],["饭店","fàndiàn"],["用","yòng"],["大","dà"],["圆桌","yuánzhuō","round table"],"，",["中间","zhōngjiān"],["还","hái"],["有","yǒu"],["一","yī"],["个","gè"],["可以","kěyǐ"],["转","zhuàn"],["的","de"],["玻璃","bōli","glass"],["台","tái"],"，",["这样","zhèyàng"],["每","měi"],["个","gè"],["人","rén"],["都","dōu"],["能","néng"],["方便","fāngbiàn"],["地","de"],["夹","jiā","to pick up (with chopsticks)"],["到","dào"],["每","měi"],["一","yī"],["道","dào"],["菜","cài"],"。"]}],"zh":"和很多西方国家不一样，中国人吃饭的时候，一般不是每人一份，而是把几个菜放在桌子中间，大家一起吃。所以，点菜的时候要考虑每个人的口味，最好有肉、有鱼、有蔬菜，再来一个汤。很多饭店用大圆桌，中间还有一个可以转的玻璃台，这样每个人都能方便地夹到每一道菜。"}
{"type":"p","id":"tb-2","segs":[{"en":"Chopsticks also come with some rules.","tok":[["用","yòng"],["筷子","kuàizi"],["也","yě"],["有","yǒu"],["一些","yīxiē"],["规矩","guīju","rules, etiquette"],"。"]},{"en":"For example, don't stand your chopsticks upright in a bowl of rice: it looks like incense offered to the dead and is considered unlucky.","tok":[["比如","bǐrú"],"，",["不要","bùyào"],["把","bǎ"],["筷子","kuàizi"],["竖","shù","upright"],["着","zhe"],["插","chā","to stick in"],["在","zài"],["米饭","mǐfàn"],["里","lǐ"],"，",["因为","yīnwèi"],["这样","zhèyàng"],["看","kàn"],["起来","qǐlai"],["很","hěn"],["像","xiàng"],["给","gěi"],["去世","qùshì"],["的","de"],["人","rén"],["上香","shàngxiāng","to offer incense","J"],"，",["会","huì"],["让","ràng"],["人","rén"],["觉得","juéde"],["不","bù"],["吉利","jílì","lucky"],"。"]},{"en":"Nor should you tap your bowl with your chopsticks, which is rude.","tok":[["也","yě"],["不要","bùyào"],["用","yòng"],["筷子","kuàizi"],["敲","qiāo","to knock"],["碗","wǎn"],"，",["这样","zhèyàng"],["很","hěn"],["不","bù"],["礼貌","lǐmào","polite"],"。"]},{"en":"When hosting, the host often puts food into the guests' bowls, a sign of warm hospitality.","tok":[["请客","qǐngkè"],["的","de"],["时候","shíhou"],"，",["主人","zhǔrén"],["常常","chángcháng"],["会","huì"],["给","gěi"],["客人","kèrén"],["夹","jiā","to pick up (with chopsticks)"],["菜","cài"],"，",["这","zhè"],["是","shì"],["热情","rèqíng"],["的","de"],["表现","biǎoxiàn"],"。"]}],"zh":"用筷子也有一些规矩。比如，不要把筷子竖着插在米饭里，因为这样看起来很像给去世的人上香，会让人觉得不吉利。也不要用筷子敲碗，这样很不礼貌。请客的时候，主人常常会给客人夹菜，这是热情的表现。"}
{"type":"p","id":"tb-3","segs":[{"en":"In China, when friends finish a meal together, they often compete to pay the bill.","tok":[["在","zài"],["中国","Zhōngguó"],"，",["朋友","péngyou"],["一起","yīqǐ"],["吃","chī"],["完","wán"],["饭","fàn"],"，",["常常","chángcháng"],["会","huì"],["抢","qiǎng","to scramble (to do sth)"],["着","zhe"],["付","fù"],["钱","qián"],"。"]},{"en":"If a friend treats you this time, it is best if you pay next time.","tok":[["如果","rúguǒ"],["这","zhè"],["次","cì"],["朋友","péngyou"],["请","qǐng"],["了","le"],["你","nǐ"],"，",["下","xià"],["次","cì"],["最好","zuìhǎo"],["由","yóu"],["你","nǐ"],["来","lái"],["请","qǐng"],"。"]},{"en":"With this give and take, friendships grow stronger and stronger.","tok":[["这样","zhèyàng"],["你来我往","nǐ lái wǒ wǎng","give and take","I"],"，",["朋友","péngyou"],["之间","zhījiān"],["的","de"],["关系","guānxì"],["就","jiù"],["会","huì"],["越来越","yuèláiyuè"],["好","hǎo"],"。"]}],"zh":"在中国，朋友一起吃完饭，常常会抢着付钱。如果这次朋友请了你，下次最好由你来请。这样你来我往，朋友之间的关系就会越来越好。"}
{"type":"p","id":"tb-4","segs":[{"en":"At more formal dinners, the seating has its rules too.","tok":[["在","zài"],["比较","bǐjiào"],["正式","zhèngshì"],["的","de"],["饭局","fànjú","formal dinner"],"，",["座位","zuòwèi"],["也","yě"],["有","yǒu"],["讲究","jiǎngjiu","particular rules"],"。"]},{"en":"Generally, the seat directly facing the door is for the host or the most important guest.","tok":[["一般","yībān"],["来说","láishuō"],"，",["正","zhèng"],["对","duì"],["着","zhe"],["门","mén"],["的","de"],["位子","wèizi","seat"],["是","shì"],["给","gěi"],["主人","zhǔrén"],["或者","huòzhě"],["最","zuì"],["重要","zhòngyào"],["的","de"],["客人","kèrén"],["坐","zuò"],["的","de"],"。"]},{"en":"If you don't know where to sit, it is best to wait for the host to seat you.","tok":[["如果","rúguǒ"],["你","nǐ"],["不","bù"],["知道","zhīdào"],["应该","yīnggāi"],["坐","zuò"],["在","zài"],["哪里","nǎli"],"，",["最好","zuìhǎo"],["等","děng"],["主人","zhǔrén"],["来","lái"],["安排","ānpái"],"。"]}],"zh":"在比较正式的饭局，座位也有讲究。一般来说，正对着门的位子是给主人或者最重要的客人坐的。如果你不知道应该坐在哪里，最好等主人来安排。"}
{"type":"h2","id":"h-street","segs":[{"en":"Street Food","tok":[["街头","jiētóu","street"],["小吃","xiǎochī","snacks","J"]]}],"zh":"街头小吃"}
{"type":"p","id":"st-1","segs":[{"en":"Besides restaurant dishes, Chinese street food is great fun too.","tok":[["除了","chúle"],["饭店","fàndiàn"],["里","lǐ"],["的","de"],["菜","cài"],"，",["中国","Zhōngguó"],["的","de"],["街头","jiētóu","street"],["小吃","xiǎochī","snacks","J"],["也","yě"],["非常","fēicháng"],["有意思","yǒuyìsi"],"。"]},{"en":"In the morning, many people buy a jianbing guozi — a savoury crepe wrapped round fried dough — or a few buns at the roadside and eat on their way to work.","tok":[["早上","zǎoshang"],"，",["很多","hěnduō"],["人","rén"],["在","zài"],["路边","lùbiān","roadside"],["买","mǎi"],["一","yī"],["个","gè"],["煎饼果子","jiānbing guǒzi","savoury crepe with fried dough","J"],["或者","huòzhě"],["几","jǐ"],["个","gè"],["包子","bāozi","steamed stuffed buns"],"，",["一边","yībiān"],["走","zǒu"],["一边","yībiān"],["吃","chī"],"，",["就","jiù"],["去","qù"],["上班","shàngbān"],["了","le"],"。"]},{"en":"In the evening, night markets offer grilled skewers, fried rice, stinky tofu and all kinds of sweets, and are crowded and lively.","tok":[["到","dào"],["了","le"],["晚上","wǎnshang"],"，",["夜市","yèshì","night market","J"],["里","lǐ"],["有","yǒu"],["烤串","kǎochuàn","grilled skewers","J"],"、",["炒饭","chǎofàn","fried rice"],"、",["臭豆腐","chòudòufu","stinky tofu","J"],["和","hé"],["各种","gèzhǒng"],["甜品","tiánpǐn","desserts"],"，",["人","rén"],["很","hěn"],["多","duō"],"，",["非常","fēicháng"],["热闹","rènao","lively"],"。"]}],"zh":"除了饭店里的菜，中国的街头小吃也非常有意思。早上，很多人在路边买一个煎饼果子或者几个包子，一边走一边吃，就去上班了。到了晚上，夜市里有烤串、炒饭、臭豆腐和各种甜品，人很多，非常热闹。"}
{"type":"p","id":"st-2","segs":[{"en":"Stinky tofu is a very special snack: it smells awful but tastes delicious.","tok":[["臭豆腐","chòudòufu","stinky tofu","J"],["是","shì"],["一","yī"],["种","zhǒng"],["很","hěn"],["特别","tèbié"],["的","de"],["小吃","xiǎochī","snacks","J"],"，",["闻","wén"],["起来","qǐlai"],["很","hěn"],["臭","chòu","smelly"],"，",["吃","chī"],["起来","qǐlai"],["却","què"],["很","hěn"],["香","xiāng"],"。"]},{"en":"Many people don't dare try it at first, but once they have, they never forget the taste.","tok":[["很多","hěnduō"],["人","rén"],["第一","dìyī"],["次","cì"],["不","bù"],["敢","gǎn"],["吃","chī"],"，",["可是","kěshì"],["尝","cháng","to taste"],["过","guo"],["一","yī"],["次","cì"],["以后","yǐhòu"],"，",["就","jiù"],["再","zài"],["也","yě"],["忘不了","wàngbuliǎo","can't forget"],["它","tā"],["的","de"],["味道","wèidao"],"。"]},{"en":"On Beijing's streets in winter you often see people selling tanghulu.","tok":[["冬天","dōngtiān"],["的","de"],["北京","Běijīng"],["街头","jiētóu","street"],"，",["常常","chángcháng"],["能","néng"],["看到","kàndào"],["卖","mài"],["糖葫芦","tánghúlu","candied haws on a stick","J"],["的","de"],["人","rén"],"。"]},{"en":"Tanghulu are hawthorn berries threaded on a bamboo stick and coated in a layer of hard sugar; sweet and sour, they are loved by adults and children alike.","tok":[["糖葫芦","tánghúlu","candied haws on a stick","J"],["是","shì"],["把","bǎ"],["山楂","shānzhā","hawthorn fruit","J"],["穿","chuān"],["在","zài"],["一","yī"],["根","gēn"],["竹签","zhúqiān","bamboo skewer"],["上","shàng"],"，",["外面","wàimiàn"],["包","bāo"],["上","shàng"],["一","yī"],["层","céng"],["糖","táng"],"，",["吃","chī"],["起来","qǐlai"],["酸酸甜甜","suānsuāntiántián","sweet and sour"],["的","de"],"，",["大人","dàrén"],["和","hé"],["孩子","háizi"],["都","dōu"],["喜欢","xǐhuan"],"。"]}],"zh":"臭豆腐是一种很特别的小吃，闻起来很臭，吃起来却很香。很多人第一次不敢吃，可是尝过一次以后，就再也忘不了它的味道。冬天的北京街头，常常能看到卖糖葫芦的人。糖葫芦是把山楂穿在一根竹签上，外面包上一层糖，吃起来酸酸甜甜的，大人和孩子都喜欢。"}
{"type":"p","id":"st-3","segs":[{"en":"Xi'an is another city full of snacks.","tok":[["西安","Xī'ān","Xi'an","N"],["也","yě"],["是","shì"],["一","yī"],["个","gè"],["小吃","xiǎochī","snacks","J"],["很","hěn"],["多","duō"],["的","de"],["城市","chéngshì"],"。"]},{"en":"The most famous are roujiamo, meat stuffed into flatbread, and yangrou paomo, mutton soup with pieces of bread.","tok":[["那里","nàli"],["最","zuì"],["有名","yǒumíng"],["的","de"],["是","shì"],["肉夹馍","ròujiāmó","meat stuffed in flatbread","J"],["和","hé"],["羊肉泡馍","yángròu pàomó","mutton soup with torn flatbread","J"],"。"]},{"en":"Roujiamo is a bit like a Chinese hamburger: meat stewed until tender is chopped and stuffed into a baked flatbread.","tok":[["肉夹馍","ròujiāmó","meat stuffed in flatbread","J"],["有点儿","yǒudiǎnr"],["像","xiàng"],["中国","Zhōngguó"],["的","de"],["汉堡","hànbǎo","hamburger"],"：",["把","bǎ"],["炖","dùn","to stew"],["得","de"],["很","hěn"],["软","ruǎn","soft, tender"],["的","de"],["肉","ròu"],["切","qiē"],["碎","suì","in small pieces"],"，",["夹","jiā","to pick up (with chopsticks)"],["在","zài"],["一","yī"],["个","gè"],["烤","kǎo","to bake, to roast"],["过","guo"],["的","de"],["饼","bǐng","flatbread"],["里","lǐ"],"。"]},{"en":"For yangrou paomo, diners first tear the bread into tiny pieces themselves and hand the bowl to the cook, who then cooks it with mutton broth.","tok":[["吃","chī"],["羊肉泡馍","yángròu pàomó","mutton soup with torn flatbread","J"],["的","de"],["时候","shíhou"],"，",["客人","kèrén"],["要","yào"],["先","xiān"],["自己","zìjǐ"],["把","bǎ"],["饼","bǐng","flatbread"],["掰","bāi","to break off (with fingers)"],["成","chéng"],["很","hěn"],["小","xiǎo"],["的","de"],["块","kuài"],"，",["然后","ránhòu"],["交","jiāo"],["给","gěi"],["厨师","chúshī","chef, cook"],"，",["厨师","chúshī","chef, cook"],["再","zài"],["把","bǎ"],["它","tā"],["和","hé"],["羊肉","yángròu"],["汤","tāng"],["一起","yīqǐ"],["煮","zhǔ","to boil"],"。"]},{"en":"Many say that the smaller you tear the pieces, the better it tastes.","tok":[["很多","hěnduō"],["人","rén"],["说","shuō"],"，",["掰","bāi","to break off (with fingers)"],["得","de"],["越","yuè"],["小","xiǎo"],"，",["吃","chī"],["起来","qǐlai"],["就","jiù"],["越","yuè"],["香","xiāng"],"。"]}],"zh":"西安也是一个小吃很多的城市。那里最有名的是肉夹馍和羊肉泡馍。肉夹馍有点儿像中国的汉堡：把炖得很软的肉切碎，夹在一个烤过的饼里。吃羊肉泡馍的时候，客人要先自己把饼掰成很小的块，然后交给厨师，厨师再把它和羊肉汤一起煮。很多人说，掰得越小，吃起来就越香。"}
{"type":"h2","id":"h-end","segs":[{"en":"In Closing","tok":[["结语","jiéyǔ","concluding remarks"]]}],"zh":"结语"}
{"type":"p","id":"end","segs":[{"en":"There are so many kinds of Chinese food that you might not get through them all in a lifetime.","tok":[["中国","Zhōngguó"],["菜","cài"],["的","de"],["种类","zhǒnglèi"],["实在","shízài"],["太","tài"],["多","duō"],["了","le"],"，",["一辈子","yībèizi","a lifetime"],["可能","kěnéng"],["也","yě"],["吃","chī"],["不","bù"],["完","wán"],"。"]},{"en":"The food of each place is bound up with its weather, landscape, history and way of life.","tok":[["每","měi"],["个","gè"],["地方","dìfang"],["的","de"],["菜","cài"],"，",["都","dōu"],["和","hé"],["那里","nàli"],["的","de"],["天气","tiānqì"],"、",["环境","huánjìng"],"、",["历史","lìshǐ"],["和","hé"],["人们","rénmen"],["的","de"],["生活","shēnghuó"],["习惯","xíguàn"],["有关","yǒuguān","to be related to"],"。"]},{"en":"So getting to know a region's food is also a good way to get to know its culture.","tok":[["所以","suǒyǐ"],"，",["了解","liǎojiě"],["一","yī"],["个","gè"],["地方","dìfang"],["的","de"],["饮食","yǐnshí","food and drink, diet"],"，",["也","yě"],["是","shì"],["了解","liǎojiě"],["那","nà"],["个","gè"],["地方","dìfang"],["文化","wénhuà"],["的","de"],["好","hǎo"],["办法","bànfǎ"],"。"]},{"en":"Next time you travel in China, don't just order the dishes you know — try the snacks the locals love best!","tok":[["下次","xiàcì"],["去","qù"],["中国","Zhōngguó"],["旅行","lǚxíng"],"，",["别","bié"],["只","zhǐ"],["点","diǎn"],["你","nǐ"],["认识","rènshi"],["的","de"],["菜","cài"],"，",["试试","shìshi"],["当地","dāngdì","local"],["人","rén"],["最","zuì"],["喜欢","xǐhuan"],["的","de"],["小吃","xiǎochī","snacks","J"],["吧","ba"],"！"]}],"zh":"中国菜的种类实在太多了，一辈子可能也吃不完。每个地方的菜，都和那里的天气、环境、历史和人们的生活习惯有关。所以，了解一个地方的饮食，也是了解那个地方文化的好办法。下次去中国旅行，别只点你认识的菜，试试当地人最喜欢的小吃吧！"}
